WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:01.100
(gentle music)

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.970
- [Narrator] This is Camp
Lemonnier in Djibouti.

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:04.860
One of the hundreds of military bases

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.720
the US has overseas.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.820
About six miles away is China's first

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.860
and only military outpost.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.330
The two superpowers say they're

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.280
in the East African country of Djibouti

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.160
to protect their security
and economic interests.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.350
And their presence goes far beyond here.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:22.440
The US has a long
established network of bases.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.330
Meanwhile, China has started expanding

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:27.180
its global military presence
at commercial ports,

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:30.493
which military experts say can
pose a challenge to the US.

00:00:30.493 --> 00:00:31.470
(gentle music)

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:33.630
So we take a look at
what's on these bases,

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.270
and compare their strategies
as China redefines

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:39.093
what it means to have a
global military footprint.

00:00:40.132 --> 00:00:41.040
(spirited upbeat music)

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.630
- [News reporter] A new
bomber base is handed over

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:43.860
to add to many others.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.330
- [Narrator] Some of
America's first foreign

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:48.240
military bases sprung
up during World War II.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:53.240
- Military base is, basically
a place where military forces

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.820
and weaponry are organized and gathered.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:57.900
- [Narrator] David Vine wrote a book

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.250
about these US facilities,

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:02.040
and has been studying them
for more than 20 years.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.100
- Foreign bases helped
militaries deploy their forces,

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.980
or have the ability to deploy their forces

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:09.450
into foreign lands.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:11.700
- [News reporter] The Japanese
launched a surprise attack.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.770
- [Narrator] After the Japanese
attack on Pearl Harbor,-

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.420
- [News reporter] Their work
had prepared one more base.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.370
- [Narrator] the US started
a construction spree

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:20.280
of military bases across
the Pacific and Europe.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.480
And when the war was over,

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:23.640
many American troops remained abroad.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:25.890
- The US government has used its military

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:30.150
including military bases,
to drive its interactions

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:32.550
with other governments and countries.

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:33.540
- [Narrator] The US has treaties

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.430
with several allies
and groups of countries

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:36.840
such as NATO that obliged

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:39.142
to ensure security in those regions.

00:01:39.142 --> 00:01:40.200
(crowd cheers)

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.150
But there's been
criticism from some locals

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:43.320
and those who see bases

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:46.492
as foreign occupation and
facilities to wage wars.

00:01:46.492 --> 00:01:47.340
(crowd cheers)

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.430
- Our armed forces stand side by side.

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:52.170
- [Narrator] The Defense
Department said in a statement

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:54.450
that it respects its host nation partners,

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:57.030
and works closely and
transparently with communities.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:59.520
Despite the controversy,
the US has kept a network

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.193
that allows American
troops to mobilize quickly.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:06.090
For instance, following
the September 11th attacks,

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:08.850
the US took over Camp
Lemonnier from France,

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:10.230
and it became a key facility

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.670
for American troops to fight

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:15.240
against Al-Shabaab, Al-Qaeda's
affiliate in Somalia.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.740
In 2018, the Pentagon said

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:19.710
the US had more than 500
bases around the world.

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.300
Though, some military researchers

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.103
and experts say there could be more.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:25.380
China on the other hand,

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.110
doesn't have a constellation
of military bases

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:29.490
because for a long time,

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:32.220
the leadership viewed it
as a sign of imperialism.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:37.200
- There had been decades of
official declaratory policy

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:41.250
from China that they would
never station forces overseas.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.170
- [Narrator] Isaac Cardin
is an assistant professor

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:45.000
at the US Naval War College,

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.160
and he's been studying
China's maritime affairs

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.660
for more than 10 years.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:51.330
- They were attempting
to position themselves

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.460
as partners of the developing world,

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:55.620
specifically against the Americans

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:57.960
who were building bases.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:02:59.460
- [Narrator] The Beijing's policies began

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:01.380
to shift in the early 2010s

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.960
as China's economic
footprint began to grow.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.640
In the first decade of this century,

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:09.000
the country's share in global
trade has almost tripled.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.650
- The leadership in Beijing recognized

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:12.900
that the scope and intensity

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.250
of China's interests overseas

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.710
required some more military capability.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.020
- [Narrator] One of those
places was in the Gulf of Aden,

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:21.270
where the rise of Somali
piracy post threats

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.710
to global shipping.

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:24.240
This is a route that China relies

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:27.240
on to ship goods between the
mainland and the Mediterranean.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:32.040
So in 2016, in an effort
to counter piracy,

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.870
Beijing said it would set up in Djibouti,

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:35.820
what it called an army support base.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:38.610
- Djibouti is probably
most effective place

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:41.430
for the People's Liberation Army

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:44.430
to start standing itself up outside

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:47.040
of China's immediate region.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.410
- [Narrator] Given the mission
to facilitate sea operations,

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.210
the Chinese base is equipped differently

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:52.590
from Camp Lemonnier.

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:54.570
It's first and foremost a naval base.

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:56.820
So China built a pier from scratch.

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:58.680
Military experts say it's large enough

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.750
to host various vessels in its fleet

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:04.083
including aircraft carriers,
destroyers, and submarines.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:06.990
The site is about 90 acres,

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:09.150
and military experts estimate it can host

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:11.100
about 2000 personnel.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.080
Just compare that with Camp Lemonnier.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:15.960
The American site is
approximately five times larger,

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.660
and can house about double the personnel.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.220
It not only has naval support,

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.830
but also land and air
forces that can participate

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:25.440
in military exercises and conflicts.

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:27.990
And the bigger size also
means the US spends more

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:30.510
on paying for the location than China.

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:32.010
It pays the Djiboutian government

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:35.580
about $63 million annually
to rent the place,

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:38.370
according to an independent
security think tank.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:40.680
While China hasn't
disclosed financial details,

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:43.567
a report by the US Congressional
Research Service says,

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:47.730
"It costs about 20 million
per year to lease the site."

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:48.930
Besides Camp Lemonnier,

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:51.600
the US has even bigger overseas spaces

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.240
that can house more than 30,000 people,

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.670
and they're usually called Little America.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:05:01.020
- It has at least four
schools, a hospital,

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:04.140
fast food facilities, a giant mall,

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:09.140
and all the trappings of a
significant US town or city.

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:11.340
- [Narrator] China's
single base falls short

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:14.250
in terms of the size and
scope of what the US has,

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:16.080
but Beijing also uses a system

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:17.820
of more than 90 commercial ports

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:20.160
and terminals outside of China.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:23.040
It's not unusual for
countries, including the US

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:24.780
to use them to dock naval vessels

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:27.090
for repairs and to resupply.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.040
- What is unusual is that China is able

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:31.020
to use commercial
facilities that are owned

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:35.250
and operated mostly by
state-owned enterprises.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:37.890
So the PLA has been granted some type

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:40.050
of preferential access to it.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:41.580
- Cardin says most of the ports

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:44.010
are partially controlled by Chinese firms,

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.920
meaning they own or operate
one or more terminals.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:50.070
But all this can still
provide a unique advantage.

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:53.820
- China's amassing
incredible stockpiles of data

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.730
about global trade on the basis

00:05:56.730 --> 00:06:00.078
of its position in
commercial ports worldwide.

00:06:00.078 --> 00:06:01.830
(jet whooshes)

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:02.870
- Cardin says this insight

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:05.100
alongside a military presence

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:07.080
can be a powerful combination

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:09.450
that could challenge
the US and its allies.

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:11.760
- When you consider
that China's potentially

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:14.940
in a position to deny,
or delay, or disrupt,

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:17.640
or even control vital shipments,

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.530
so ultimately this network puts them

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:22.769
in a position where they
have some coercive leverage.

00:06:22.769 --> 00:06:23.602
(bell rings)

00:06:23.602 --> 00:06:25.560
- [Narrator] For now,
military experts say China

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:28.500
isn't pursuing an extensive
network like the US.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:29.580
The concerns have been growing

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.110
among some American officials

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:33.810
that Beijing could be planning new Bases.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:37.290
- They are seeking, actively
seeking a military base

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:39.690
on the Atlantic coast of Africa.

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:41.550
The place where they've
actually made progress

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:43.754
toward this is equatorial Guinea.

00:06:43.754 --> 00:06:45.180
(gentle music)

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:47.010
- [Narrator] China's defense
ministry didn't respond

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:50.070
to a request for comment on
its base plans in Africa,

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:52.230
or whether Beijing could
use commercial ports

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:54.330
to counter other countries.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.490
The US Defense Department
said it's concerned

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:57.960
about the lack of transparency

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:00.510
and clarity around Beijing's negotiations

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:02.550
with host nations.

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:05.760
So as the US and China
compete for global influence,

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:06.930
the networks that they build

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:08.430
and maintain could become one

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:10.625
of their most essential military assets.

00:07:10.625 --> 00:07:13.208
(gentle music)

